[0] A3 pole factor - (11/3-2L+ell) = 0
[1] int_lam^{1-lam} P dt = -2*log(lambda) - 11/6
    restriction t < V-1 is inactive for V > 2 (daughters of the produced gluon have p+ < k+ < vee-k+)
[2] UV sum = log((V - 1)/V)/2 ; L parts: {'Row II': -1, 'Row V': 2, 'norm UV': -1, 'coupling CT': 0}
[3] (a) restricted FF CT only, R1 (P_gg on [0,1] applied to theta(xi>k+/vee) Pi) : IR sum = 0 ; two-eps total = log((V - 1)/V)/2 ; single-eps total = log((V - 1)/V)/2
[3] (a) restricted FF CT only, R2 (plus subtraction on [k+/vee,1]) : IR sum = log(V) - log(V - 1) ; two-eps total = -log((V - 1)/V)/2 ; single-eps total = -log((V - 1)/V)/2
[4] (b) + range-restricted coupling CT (norm. UV half with p+<vee-k+): identical to (a) for vee>2k+, since [1] is unchanged;
    leftover at finite vee, eps->0 first: (ell/2)(2/eps) [R1] or -(ell/2)(2/eps) [R2], ell=log(1-k+/vee)=-k+/vee+O((k+/vee)^2)
